  "behavior": [
    "WalletConnect uses the shared signing review with captured session origin, account/address and exact network/chain. Current wallet/catalog selection cannot replace admission context. The removed summary no longer truncates messages or addresses or displays gas units as a fee.",
    "The adapter checks captured context, canonical HTTP(S) origin, topic/peer/revision, chain and method-defined signer. Missing or mismatched legacy context blocks approval. The worker independently retains its live session, provider and account authorization checks.",
    "Readable messages and strict typed data are shown completely; typed Boolean false remains false. All EVM transactions retain blind-signing treatment, including empty calldata. Native amount, full destination and a computed execution-fee limit are shown when available; complete raw chain/method/params remain scrollable.",
    "Blind requests require raw expansion and explicit risk acknowledgement. Request replacement resets consent synchronously; flagged or invalid verification offers Close only, and malformed context has no Approve action. Unknown verification is labelled Unverified.",
    "Approval/rejection retain the captured approval ID, method-defined signer, pending exclusion, stale-DOM guard, retry and empty-queue behavior. Transport callbacks stay in the WalletConnect wrapper so ordinary signing has no runtime-messaging import side effect.",
    "The shared view places action failures beside controls and brings them into view only while the same request remains active. Empty-route navigation errors remain visible. Russian sender/recipient labels are supplied; the WalletConnect brand is an intentional template literal."
  ],
